# Mission plan

## Objectives

1. Resolve the target **registered** documentation folder from
   **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`** (slug → `localPath`).
2. Gather source-of-truth inputs via exactly one intake path:
   **documents** (file or folder), **brainstorm** with the user, or an
   **existing agent plan**.
3. Produce a reviewable **SoT change plan** naming creates/updates under
   **`<localPath>/source-of-truth/`**.
4. Write SoT files **only** after explicit user approval per
   [`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/20_source-of-truth.mdc`](../../rules/20_source-of-truth.mdc)
   write authority — approved paths only.
5. After each approved SoT write pass, append entries to
   **`<localPath>/source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`** per rule **20** § *Change log
   (audit only)* — for auditing and review only. Do **not** treat the change
   log as authoritative SoT unless the user explicitly refers to it and
   explains how to use it.
6. When hosting-tracked changes are required (registry, `.gitignore`,
   `.cursorignore` indexing), ship via hosting-repo worktree → commit → PR →
   merge. SoT **payload** stays under the gitignored documentation tree;
   sync with **rclone** when the user confirms.
7. Close the dispatch with an explicit Squad Leader resolution proposal when
   SoT work is complete, deferred, or abandoned.

## Squad operations (three-lane hosting-repo delivery)

Use when a later **improve / expand / fix** pass on **this mission** ships
**substantive hosting-repo** changes through PRs. Runtime SoT authoring on this
mission follows **Protocol** §§1–8 below (not three-lane by default).

Normative contract: [`.sedea/centers/sedea/docs/mission-three-lane-cadence.md`](.sedea/centers/sedea/docs/mission-three-lane-cadence.md).

**Roles (when three-lane active)**

| Role | Lane | `execution` | Spawns | Does not |
|------|------|-------------|--------|----------|
| **Squad Leader** | Dispatch leader | — | Requirements → Planning → Implement skill paths under `skills/` | Inline planning skills on leader |
| **Requirements author** | Child lane 1 | `spawned` | — | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution` |
| **Planning agent** | Child lane 2 | `spawned` | Inline `pr-breakdown`, `new-plan`, `pr-plan` on this lane | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution` |
| **Implementation agent** | Child lane 3 | `spawned` | — | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution` |

**Planning constraints (binding when three-lane active):** one phase only · PR breakdown only (≤3 PRs) · complexity ≤12 · forbid `delivery-phases` / `phase-planner`.

**Next stop after PR exists (Squad Leader — binding when three-lane active):** when an implement lane opens a hosting-repo PR on this mission's ship chain, open **#external-wait** structured choice **before ending the turn** — do **not** prose-only *tell me when you've checked GitHub*. Required options **in this order**:

| Option id | Label |
|-----------|-------|
| `approve-merge-pr` | Approve and Merge PR |
| `merged-pr-proceed` | PR merged — verify and proceed |
| `start-pr-review` | Start inline PR review |
| `check-pr-status` | Check PR merge status |
| `defer` | Defer next ship step |
| `more-details` | More details for option _ |

**Supersession (binding):** [rule **6** § *PR approve-merge structured choice*](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/6_git-commit-push-gate.mdc) **supersedes** abbreviated external-wait examples elsewhere in this plan when the PR is open and org policy allows agent merge.

**After PR open — merge paths:** When agent merge is offered, **`approve-merge-pr`** (label **Approve and Merge PR**) is **option index 1** per [`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/6_git-commit-push-gate.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/6_git-commit-push-gate.mdc) § *PR approve-merge structured choice*; **`merged-pr-proceed`** (when present) is **option index 2**. **Default without agent merge pick:** user merge on GitHub; lane verifies via **`merged-pr-proceed`**. On **`approve-merge-pr`**, run rule **6** § *Merge inspect procedure* before **`gh pr review --approve`** or **`gh pr merge`** — **forbidden** to merge without that same-turn pick or to copy **`promote-center-submodule-pin`** auto-merge.

**Merge act (binding):** On **`approve-merge-pr`**, and only after that same-turn pick, run [rule **6** § *Merge inspect procedure*](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/6_git-commit-push-gate.mdc) before mutating GitHub. On **`merged-pr-proceed`**, use **`gh pr view`** only to verify merge state — do **not** mutate GitHub.

**Dispatch display refresh (Squad Leader).** When dispatch scope is readable on the leader lane (matched command phrase, resolved folder slug, or scope title), call MCP **`mission_control_update_dispatch_display`** with non-empty **`dispatchTitle`** (≤64 chars) and optional **`dispatchDescription`** / **`dispatchHoverDescription`** (≤512 chars). **Skip** when chrome already matches. **Forbidden:** **`mission_control_update_lane_display`** to relabel **child** slots from the leader lane; hand-editing **`dispatch-tab.v1.json`**. **Title content (binding):** topic/domain of the **whole dispatch** only — **not** live sync status. See [`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/9_display-metadata-authority.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/9_display-metadata-authority.mdc) § *Dispatch title content*.

## Protocol

### 1. Infer intent from the opening command phrase

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Match command phrases and prepare routing.
- **Inputs:** Opening message; **`mission.yaml`** `commands`.
- **Expected output:** Intent label (`author` | `refresh`).
- **Next-step resolution:** Phrase matches → §2 (auto-advance). No match → USER_CHECKPOINT below.

USER_CHECKPOINT — confirm author vs refresh when the opening command phrase does not match unambiguously.

- Apply **phrase matching** from [`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc) (longer phrases first).
- Map phrases from **`mission.yaml`**:
  - **`author source of truth`** → intent **`author`**
  - **`refresh source of truth`** → intent **`refresh`**
- After intent is mapped, when dispatch scope is readable, run **Dispatch display refresh** — skip when chrome already matches.

### 2. Resolve registered documentation folder

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Bind work to one registered folder slug and its `localPath`.
- **Inputs:** Opening message remainder; **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`**.
- **Expected output:** `folderSlug`, `localPath`, whether `<localPath>/source-of-truth/` already exists.
- **Next-step resolution:** Folder clear → §3. Not clear → USER_CHECKPOINT below.

USER_CHECKPOINT — pick registered folder slug when the opening message does not name one.

- Read the registry; list folders with slug + `localPath`.
- Validate `localPath` exists on disk (or stop with a clear gap — may need **configure new documentation folder** on a new dispatch).
- Record whether **`source-of-truth/`** is present (informs `author` vs `refresh` expectations).
- Re-run **Dispatch display refresh** when the folder slug improves the title.

### 2a. Always-on Sync GDrive folder on Squad Leader structured choice (binding)

After §2 folder bind succeeds, **every** Squad Leader
**`mission_control_present_structured_choice`** / **AskQuestion** modal on this
dispatch **must** include **Sync GDrive folder** until dispatch resolution.

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Option id** | `sync-gdrive-folder` |
| **Label** | Sync GDrive folder |
| **Placement** | After mission-specific options; **before** the universal modal trailer per rule **2** |

**Applies to:** §3 intake gate; §4 gather checkpoints; §5 SoT plan approval;
§7 sync/ship gate; §8 resolution gate; **#external-wait** resume modals on the
**leader** lane — any Squad Leader gate after §2 folder bind.

**Forbidden:** omitting `sync-gdrive-folder` from any Squad Leader modal after
§2 folder bind; treating sync as available only at §7 after a write pass.

**On select `sync-gdrive-folder`:** run §7 **rclone sync** branch (registered
folder per center registry / rclone contract). On success, **re-open the same
gate** that was active when sync started. User may sync **any number of times**
during the dispatch.

### 3. Pick intake mode

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Choose how SoT source material is gathered.
- **Inputs:** Intent from §1; optional opening seeds (paths, plan `@path`).
- **Expected output:** `intakeMode`: `documents` | `brainstorm` | `existing-plan`.
- **Next-step resolution:** Mode selected → §4.

USER_CHECKPOINT — pick intake mode (documents · brainstorm · existing agent plan).

| Mode | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **`documents`** | User supplies a file or folder of source materials |
| **`brainstorm`** | Free-form research / Q&A with the user until enough context exists |
| **`existing-plan`** | User supplies an existing agent plan (`@path` or absolute path) |

### 4. Gather information

- **Type:** Simple skill execution (with early exits)
- **Intent:** Collect enough evidence to draft a SoT change plan.
- **Inputs:** `intakeMode`; folder binding from §2; source paths or plan path when applicable.
- **Expected output:** Gathered notes / excerpt ledger sufficient for §5 (paths read, decisions, gaps).
- **Next-step resolution:** Enough context → §5. Blocked (unreadable path, empty materials) → USER_CHECKPOINT below.

**Procedure by mode**

1. **`documents`** — Read supplied file(s) or folder; build a source ledger. Do not invent content from titles alone.
2. **`brainstorm`** — Ask structured questions; accumulate answers until the user confirms gathering is complete.
3. **`existing-plan`** — Read the plan; extract SoT-relevant scope; note out-of-scope items.

**Document extraction (binding — `documents` intake)**

When **`documents`** intake includes `.pdf` or other non-plaintext files, apply
**`rules/10_required-tools.mdc`** § *Document extraction during gathers* before
drafting §5:

1. Identify type with `file`.
2. **PDF on macOS:** run center **`scripts/pdf-extract.jxa`** (or equivalent
   JXA + PDFKit) — **default** text extract; do not use `textutil` on PDF.
3. **Office / RTF / HTML:** `textutil -convert txt -stdout` before any Python
   stack.
4. Missing **registry** tool (`rclone`, …) → stop; tell the user to start
   **`install required tools`** on a **new dispatch** — do not `pip install`
   mid-gather.
5. Empty PDF text (likely scanned/image-only) or extract failure → USER_CHECKPOINT
   below; **forbidden:** silent `pip install pypdf` / `brew install poppler`
   without developer pick.

Cross-ref: [documentation-management#60](https://github.com/sedea-centers/documentation-management/issues/60)
(premature pip during SoT gather).

When **`source-of-truth/`** already exists, consult it as the sole default authority for current SoT state per rule **20** — do not treat other folder paths as authoritative unless the user explicitly expands scope.

**Change log:** Do **not** consult **`source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`** as
authoritative SoT state during gather/plan/author. Open it only when the user
explicitly names the change log and states how to use it for this turn (rule **20**).

USER_CHECKPOINT — retry paths · switch intake mode · pause when gathering cannot proceed.

### 5. Draft SoT change plan

- **Type:** Branching logic + authoring confirmation
- **Intent:** Produce an explicit plan of SoT file creates/updates before any write.
- **Inputs:** Gathered materials; existing `source-of-truth/` tree when present.
- **Expected output:** Approved SoT change plan (file list + one-line purpose each; create vs update).
- **Next-step resolution:** Approved → §6. Revise → re-draft. Defer → pause.

USER_CHECKPOINT — approve SoT change plan before writing any `source-of-truth/` files.

Present in one turn: delta + full plan in **`displayMarkdown`**, then structured choice (approve · revise · pause · More details for option _).

**Forbidden:** writing SoT files before this approval; unilateral “keep SoT in sync.”

### 6. Write source-of-truth

- **Type:** Simple skill execution
- **Intent:** Apply only approved SoT paths under **`<localPath>/source-of-truth/`**.
- **Inputs:** Approved change plan from §5.
- **Expected output:** Files written/updated exactly as approved; short write
  recap; `changelogPath`; `changelogAppended: true` (or honest skip reason if no
  SoT content paths changed).
- **Next-step resolution:** Writes done → §7.

- Create **`source-of-truth/`** when missing and the plan includes creates.
- Edit **only** approved paths. Do not delete or rewrite unrelated SoT files.
- Directory name must be exactly **`source-of-truth`** (kebab-case) per rule **20**.
- **Change log (binding):** After approved SoT content paths are written,
  append matching entries to **`<localPath>/source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md`**
  (create the file if missing) per rule **20** § *Change log (audit only)*.
  Minimum: ISO date, paths touched, change summary, approval locus
  (`author source of truth` / `refresh source of truth` + folder slug).
- **Forbidden:** treating the write pass complete without the change-log
  append when SoT content paths changed; consulting **`CHANGELOG.md`** as
  default SoT on later gathers in this or other missions.

### 7. Sync and optional hosting-repo ship

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Persist documentation payload remotely when needed; ship hosting-tracked edits only when this pass changed them.
- **Inputs:** Write recap; whether hosting-tracked files changed this pass.
- **Expected output:** Sync status and/or hosting PR URL when applicable.
- **Next-step resolution:** Complete → §8.

USER_CHECKPOINT — rclone sync now · skip sync · start hosting ship (when tracked files changed) · More details for option _.

**§2a cross-ref (binding):** When sync is invoked via **`sync-gdrive-folder`**
from any earlier gate, run the **rclone sync** branch here, then re-open that
gate — not only at end-of-write-pass.

| Branch | When | Action |
|--------|------|--------|
| **rclone sync** | User confirms | Sync registered folder per center registry / rclone contract |
| **Skip sync** | User defers remote | Record local SoT done; note sync remaining |
| **Hosting ship** | This pass edited hosting-tracked files | Hosting-repo ship cadence below — worktree (if needed) → commit/push/PR → inline **`pr-review`** until terminal → post-PR merge paths → post-merge cleanup |

**Hosting-repo ship cadence (when applicable):** [`.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/worktree-setup/SKILL.md`](.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/worktree-setup/SKILL.md) → rule **6** pipeline → [`.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md`](.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md) → **Post-PR merge paths** (below) → [`.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/worktree-cleanup/SKILL.md`](.sedea/centers/sedea/skills/worktree-cleanup/SKILL.md).

